      "message": "This fix seems inoccuous enough, but the fact that `onChange` is getting called for a URI that we didn\u0027t register as an observer of is suspicious to me, and I think this fix may mask an underlying issue. Can you log the URI when your Monkey test fails, so that we can work out what\u0027s going on?\n\nFrom a quick look at the code, I wonder if this is because we pass `true` for `notifyForDescendants` when calling [`registerContentObserver`](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/content/ContentResolver#registerContentObserver(android.net.Uri,%20boolean,%20android.database.ContentObserver)) in `registerAndUpdate` (line 123). That\u0027s the only way I can see that we might get change notifications for a URI that we don\u0027t have an observer for. It might be worth trying setting that parameter to `false` and seeing if that fixes your test, instead.",
